1
00:00:01,280 --> 00:00:02,617
What are you talking about?

2
00:00:02,700 --> 00:00:06,037
Why should we have to share
these healing crystals with you?

3
00:00:06,120 --> 00:00:08,767
Your pet lizard has
healing powers, you know.

4
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:12,517
But you never fight on the front
line, so who are you to talk?

5
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:14,659
You don't need to use any crystals.

6
00:00:15,020 --> 00:00:15,957
Of course I do.

7
00:00:16,040 --> 00:00:18,477
You're the popular one
around here, Silica.

8
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:21,501
I can't expect the boys
to help me when I need it.

9
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:23,240
Oh, come on.

10
00:00:23,420 --> 00:00:24,437
It's not like that.

11
00:00:24,520 --> 00:00:25,720
Fine. I don't care.

12
00:00:26,040 --> 00:00:27,017
You want my items?

13
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:27,930
Take them.

14
00:00:28,013 --> 00:00:29,517
But I'm never going to
team up with you again.

15
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:34,541
I know there's a ton of other parties out
there who'd love to have me on their side.

16
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:36,657
Wait! Don't go!

17
00:00:36,740 --> 00:00:37,570
Silica!

18
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:55,100
I'll see you in the future,
but I'll see you in the future.

19
00:01:56,220 --> 00:01:59,100
I want to know it's the origin.

20
00:01:59,420 --> 00:02:02,160
I'll give you everything I have.

21
00:02:33,540 --> 00:02:35,187
I'm out of healing crystals!

22
00:02:53,300 --> 00:02:54,700
Inna!

23
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:56,280
Inna! Inna!

24
00:02:58,820 --> 00:02:59,797
Arrghh!

25
00:02:59,880 --> 00:03:01,280
Inna!

26
00:03:03,320 --> 00:03:04,720
Inna!

27
00:03:06,480 --> 00:03:08,060
Inna! Inna!

28
00:03:08,280 --> 00:03:09,200
Inna!

29
00:03:42,200 --> 00:03:43,030
Pina...

30
00:03:44,660 --> 00:03:47,420
Don't leave me all alone here...

31
00:03:48,420 --> 00:03:49,250
Pina!

32
00:03:53,220 --> 00:03:54,396
What's that feather?

33
00:03:55,900 --> 00:03:56,840
It's Pina.

34
00:03:57,880 --> 00:03:59,720
My best friend.

35
00:04:01,260 --> 00:04:03,907
You're one of those
beast tamers, aren't you?

36
00:04:04,440 --> 00:04:05,440
I'm sorry.

37
00:04:05,940 --> 00:04:09,058
If I got here sooner, I
could have saved your friend.

38
00:04:09,540 --> 00:04:11,680
No, it's all my fault.

39
00:04:12,260 --> 00:04:16,201
I was stupid to think I could make
it through the forest on my own.

40
00:04:17,740 --> 00:04:19,300
Thank you for saving me.

41
00:04:19,740 --> 00:04:21,093
You did what you could.

42
00:04:22,140 --> 00:04:22,970
That feather.

43
00:04:23,053 --> 00:04:25,979
Check and see if it has an
item name attached to it.

44
00:04:34,220 --> 00:04:35,380
Hey, don't cry.

45
00:04:35,580 --> 00:04:37,437
That means Pina's heart's still here.

46
00:04:37,520 --> 00:04:39,579
There's a chance you can revive it.

47
00:04:40,740 --> 00:04:41,900
No way, really?

48
00:04:42,440 --> 00:04:43,270
Mm-hmm.

49
00:04:43,353 --> 00:04:47,957
On the south side of Floor 47, there's a
field dungeon called the Hill of Memories.

50
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:52,393
I heard somewhere that the flower
growing at the top can revive familiars.

51
00:04:55,940 --> 00:04:57,300
Floor 47, huh?

52
00:04:58,720 --> 00:05:00,517
I'd offer to go get it for you.

53
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:02,697
All you'd have to do is pay for the trip.

54
00:05:02,780 --> 00:05:06,837
The thing is, the flower won't bloom
unless the familiars' master's there.

55
00:05:06,920 --> 00:05:09,391
Thank you so much for telling me about it.

56
00:05:09,740 --> 00:05:12,597
If I work hard to raise my
level, then someday I could...

57
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:15,680
Sure, but the time limit's
three days to revive it.

58
00:05:16,640 --> 00:05:17,470
No way.

59
00:05:19,180 --> 00:05:20,320
It's all my fault.

60
00:05:21,420 --> 00:05:22,980
I'm so sorry, Pina.

61
00:05:24,020 --> 00:05:24,850
It's okay.

62
00:05:25,100 --> 00:05:26,300
You have three days.

63
00:05:28,580 --> 00:05:29,756
Take this equipment.

64
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,837
It should boost you five or six levels.

65
00:05:31,920 --> 00:05:35,096
And if I tag along, I'm sure
everything will work out.

66
00:05:37,780 --> 00:05:40,020
But why would you do all this for me?

67
00:05:43,240 --> 00:05:46,652
I'll tell you, but only if you
promise not to laugh, okay?

68
00:05:47,460 --> 00:05:48,860
I promise I won't.

69
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:52,430
All right.

70
00:05:52,760 --> 00:05:55,348
It's because you look
like my little sister.

71
00:06:03,200 --> 00:06:04,080
I'm sorry.

72
00:06:07,440 --> 00:06:10,577
Mom, I know this isn't enough
cold to pay you back, but...

73
00:06:10,660 --> 00:06:11,490
No, it's cool.

74
00:06:11,900 --> 00:06:13,837
Besides, it works with why I'm here.

75
00:06:13,920 --> 00:06:15,802
We'll be helping each other out.

76
00:06:16,620 --> 00:06:17,450
Okay, then.

77
00:06:17,540 --> 00:06:18,537
My name's Silica.

78
00:06:18,620 --> 00:06:19,796
My name's Kitty-Toe.

79
00:06:20,060 --> 00:06:23,178
I guess we'll be working
together for a little while.

80
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:32,160
Hey, look! It's Silica!

81
00:06:33,120 --> 00:06:35,037
It took you a long time to get back.

82
00:06:35,120 --> 00:06:36,532
We were getting worried.

83
00:06:36,780 --> 00:06:38,257
You want to team up with us?

84
00:06:38,340 --> 00:06:40,634
We'll take you wherever you want to go.

85
00:06:40,720 --> 00:06:43,320
That's really nice of you to offer, but...

86
00:06:45,260 --> 00:06:49,142
Well, I've sort of already agreed
to be in a party with him, so...

87
00:06:51,260 --> 00:06:52,090
Okay, later.

88
00:06:52,173 --> 00:06:53,003
Bye!

89
00:06:55,580 --> 00:06:58,345
I didn't mean to put you
on the spot like that.

90
00:06:58,480 --> 00:06:59,837
Didn't know you had fans.

91
00:06:59,920 --> 00:07:01,096
You must be popular.

92
00:07:01,500 --> 00:07:02,330
No.

93
00:07:03,680 --> 00:07:05,117
They don't take me seriously.

94
00:07:05,200 --> 00:07:07,082
They want me to be their mascot.

95
00:07:09,360 --> 00:07:10,536
Maybe they're right.

96
00:07:10,720 --> 00:07:15,020
They call me Dragon Tamer, and
I guess it went to my head.

97
00:07:15,620 --> 00:07:16,860
Don't worry about it.

98
00:07:18,540 --> 00:07:19,834
We'll make it in time.

99
00:07:19,960 --> 00:07:20,790
Promise.

100
00:07:22,740 --> 00:07:23,570
Okay.

101
00:07:25,860 --> 00:07:27,742
Do you live around here, Kirito?

102
00:07:28,060 --> 00:07:29,217
I'm on floor 50.

103
00:07:29,300 --> 00:07:32,737
It's kind of far, so I was
thinking of getting a room tonight.

104
00:07:32,820 --> 00:07:35,637
If you stay, I'll take you
out for some cheesecake.

105
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:36,937
It's really good here.

106
00:07:37,020 --> 00:07:38,580
Well, if it isn't silica.

107
00:07:40,560 --> 00:07:43,080
Wow, you made it out of the forest alive.

108
00:07:43,480 --> 00:07:44,640
Good for you, girl.

109
00:07:45,660 --> 00:07:46,601
Something wrong?

110
00:07:46,780 --> 00:07:49,100
Oh, no, nothing. Hang on.

111
00:07:49,280 --> 00:07:51,617
What happened to your
little friend the lizard?

112
00:07:51,700 --> 00:07:52,940
Did it run away?

113
00:07:53,420 --> 00:07:54,800
Peanut died saving me.

114
00:07:55,100 --> 00:07:58,500
But I'm going to get Peanut back. Really?

115
00:07:59,300 --> 00:08:02,237
I guess you'll be heading for
the Hill of Memories, then.

116
00:08:02,320 --> 00:08:05,438
I wonder if you'll be able
to clear it at your level.

117
00:08:05,900 --> 00:08:07,080
Of course she will.

118
00:08:07,760 --> 00:08:09,701
It's not that difficult to level.

119
00:08:10,640 --> 00:08:13,111
Oh, God, this girl seduced another player.

120
00:08:13,760 --> 00:08:16,837
No, it's not difficult, but
you don't look that strong.

121
00:08:16,920 --> 00:08:17,750
Come on.

122
00:08:21,920 --> 00:08:23,802
Why does she have to be so mean?

123
00:08:25,580 --> 00:08:28,260
Well, is Sword Art Online your first MMO?

124
00:08:28,820 --> 00:08:29,650
Uh-huh.

125
00:08:30,160 --> 00:08:33,757
A lot of people's personalities
change when they play games online.

126
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:37,075
And some actually like playing
the game as the bad guy.

127
00:08:37,760 --> 00:08:39,760
You see how our cursors are green?

128
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:44,517
Well, if you commit a crime against another
player, your cursor's gonna turn orange.

129
00:08:44,600 --> 00:08:47,017
Then they become what's
called a red player.

130
00:08:47,100 --> 00:08:49,500
The worst, also known as player killers.

131
00:08:49,800 --> 00:08:51,271
They're all about murder.

132
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:53,412
They kill other players?

133
00:08:53,700 --> 00:08:58,177
In a normal game, they roleplay as the
bad guy, have some laughs, and it's cool.

134
00:08:58,260 --> 00:09:00,840
But, Sword Art Online isn't normal.

135
00:09:03,460 --> 00:09:05,680
It's definitely not a game.

136
00:09:07,360 --> 00:09:08,190
Kirito?

137
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:11,630
I'm sorry.

138
00:09:14,120 --> 00:09:16,437
Well, I think you're good, so...

139
00:09:16,520 --> 00:09:18,480
I mean, you saved me after all.

140
00:09:21,120 --> 00:09:23,277
Looks like you cheered me up instead.

141
00:09:23,360 --> 00:09:24,980
Thank you, Silica.

142
00:09:28,780 --> 00:09:29,610
Ah!

143
00:09:29,693 --> 00:09:31,977
Wow, where the heck is
our cheesecake already?

144
00:09:32,060 --> 00:09:34,660
Excuse me, our dessert
hasn't shown up yet!

145
00:09:41,320 --> 00:09:45,320
I wonder if he'd laugh if I told
him I wanted to talk some more.

146
00:09:46,580 --> 00:09:48,440
Silica, you still awake?

147
00:09:49,140 --> 00:09:50,360
Kirito!

148
00:09:50,680 --> 00:09:55,057
I forgot to tell you some stuff about
447, but it can wait till tomorrow.

149
00:09:55,140 --> 00:09:56,060
No, now's fine!

150
00:09:56,320 --> 00:09:59,438
Actually, I was just thinking
I should ask you about…

151
00:10:02,220 --> 00:10:03,940
That was so close!

152
00:10:06,840 --> 00:10:09,260
Uh, what's up? Something wrong?

153
00:10:10,680 --> 00:10:11,597
No, nothing!

154
00:10:11,680 --> 00:10:13,400
What's that thing do, Kirito?

155
00:10:13,880 --> 00:10:15,260
It's a mirage sphere.

156
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:25,560
It's pretty.

157
00:10:26,380 --> 00:10:28,517
This is the town area of 447.

158
00:10:28,600 --> 00:10:30,697
And that's the hill of memories.

159
00:10:30,780 --> 00:10:32,817
I was thinking if we take this route.

160
00:10:32,900 --> 00:10:33,730
We can.

161
00:10:35,060 --> 00:10:35,890
What's wrong?

162
00:10:36,580 --> 00:10:37,410
Who's there?

163
00:10:39,860 --> 00:10:40,690
Um.

164
00:10:40,773 --> 00:10:41,637
Who was it?

165
00:10:41,720 --> 00:10:43,297
An eavesdropper.

166
00:10:43,380 --> 00:10:44,557
But they can't.

167
00:10:44,640 --> 00:10:47,617
I mean, you can't hear through
a door unless you knock first.

168
00:10:47,700 --> 00:10:50,477
But if your listening skill
is high enough, you can.

169
00:10:50,560 --> 00:10:51,619
It takes practice.

170
00:10:51,960 --> 00:10:53,477
Not that many players have it.

171
00:10:53,560 --> 00:10:55,678
Why would they want to listen to us?

172
00:11:05,680 --> 00:11:06,510
Wow!

173
00:11:07,960 --> 00:11:09,700
This place is like a dream!

174
00:11:10,240 --> 00:11:11,070
I know.

175
00:11:11,153 --> 00:11:12,897
The whole floor is covered in flowers.

176
00:11:12,980 --> 00:11:15,451
That's why they call it the flower garden.

177
00:11:25,920 --> 00:11:26,750
Cumbles!

178
00:11:33,260 --> 00:11:34,600
Silica? What? Nothing!

179
00:11:35,020 --> 00:11:36,437
Sorry to keep you waiting.

180
00:11:36,520 --> 00:11:38,060
What's wrong? Oh, nothing.

181
00:11:38,280 --> 00:11:39,900
Nothing at all. Come on.

182
00:11:41,600 --> 00:11:42,430
Okay.

183
00:11:46,400 --> 00:11:47,341
What's that for?

184
00:11:47,820 --> 00:11:49,917
If anything bad happens
while we're in here,

185
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:51,777
I'm going to tell you to warp out, okay?

186
00:11:51,860 --> 00:11:53,507
When I do, use this crystal.

187
00:11:53,640 --> 00:11:55,581
You can jump to any town with it.

188
00:11:56,020 --> 00:11:57,520
But... No buts. Use it.

189
00:11:59,180 --> 00:12:00,010
I understand.

190
00:12:02,460 --> 00:12:03,401
Let's get going.

191
00:12:03,600 --> 00:12:07,482
If we take this path, it'll lead
us right to the Hill of Memories.

192
00:12:18,120 --> 00:12:19,320
Um, Kirito...

193
00:12:23,540 --> 00:12:28,397
Calm down!

194
00:12:28,480 --> 00:12:30,186
That thing's not that strong!

195
00:12:30,740 --> 00:12:34,540
Oh, Kirito, save me! But don't
look! Save me! But don't look!

196
00:12:34,700 --> 00:12:36,300
That'll be... difficult.

197
00:12:36,980 --> 00:12:38,080
D-darn you!

198
00:12:38,460 --> 00:12:39,620
Put me down!

199
00:12:55,580 --> 00:12:56,840
You see anything?

200
00:12:58,000 --> 00:12:59,000
Not really.

201
00:13:01,340 --> 00:13:05,880
I hope you don't mind me asking,
but what's your sister like?

202
00:13:06,140 --> 00:13:07,552
Why do you want to know?

203
00:13:07,660 --> 00:13:10,140
Well, you said I looked like her.

204
00:13:10,900 --> 00:13:15,660
I know it's not polite to ask about
your real life, but what's she like?

205
00:13:16,440 --> 00:13:19,820
I call her my little sister,
but she's really my cousin.

206
00:13:21,620 --> 00:13:24,457
We were raised like brother and
sister since we were babies,

207
00:13:24,540 --> 00:13:26,069
so I doubt she even knows.

208
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:30,200
But I know, and I guess that's
the reason I avoided her.

209
00:13:31,300 --> 00:13:33,182
Our grandfather's really strict.

210
00:13:33,500 --> 00:13:37,382
When I was eight, he made us take
classes at the local kendo dojo.

211
00:13:37,680 --> 00:13:40,151
But after a couple years, I stopped going.

212
00:13:40,500 --> 00:13:42,677
Grandpa beat the hell out of me for that.

213
00:13:42,760 --> 00:13:43,700
That's awful.

214
00:13:45,080 --> 00:13:48,237
Anyway, then my sister stood
up for me and told him to stop.

215
00:13:48,320 --> 00:13:50,617
She said she'd train hard for both of us.

216
00:13:50,700 --> 00:13:51,640
And she did.

217
00:13:51,840 --> 00:13:52,900
She trained hard.

218
00:13:53,100 --> 00:13:55,680
She even made it to
the Nationals. She did?

219
00:13:55,780 --> 00:13:56,610
How awesome!

220
00:13:57,820 --> 00:14:01,291
Yeah, I've always felt guilty
for putting her through that.

221
00:14:01,440 --> 00:14:03,417
I wouldn't doubt it if she hates me.

222
00:14:03,500 --> 00:14:06,500
God knows she could have
been doing something else.

223
00:14:06,640 --> 00:14:08,617
Maybe that's why I wanted to help you.

224
00:14:08,700 --> 00:14:12,112
In a weird way, it makes me
feel like I'm paying her back.

225
00:14:12,860 --> 00:14:13,700
There it is.

226
00:14:15,020 --> 00:14:17,477
If you don't mind me saying, you're wrong.

227
00:14:17,560 --> 00:14:19,619
I don't think she hates you at all.

228
00:14:19,840 --> 00:14:22,857
She wouldn't work that hard
for you if she didn't like you.

229
00:14:22,940 --> 00:14:23,770
Promise.

230
00:14:23,853 --> 00:14:25,564
And I bet she even loves Kendo.

231
00:14:27,120 --> 00:14:29,591
There you go again, making me feel better.

232
00:14:31,600 --> 00:14:32,437
Maybe you're right.

233
00:14:32,520 --> 00:14:33,660
Man, I hope so.

234
00:14:36,260 --> 00:14:37,100
Okay, then.

235
00:14:37,380 --> 00:14:39,000
I'm gonna do my best, too.

236
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:45,830
Kiriko!

237
00:15:00,700 --> 00:15:02,980
Is that reviving flower around here?

238
00:15:03,220 --> 00:15:04,300
Yeah, over there.

239
00:15:28,120 --> 00:15:29,355
Go ahead, pick it up.

240
00:15:35,820 --> 00:15:39,060
You sure it'll bring Pina
back to life? Uh-huh.

241
00:15:39,600 --> 00:15:40,640
I'm so glad.

242
00:15:41,080 --> 00:15:43,777
There's a bunch of strong
monsters lurking around here.

243
00:15:43,860 --> 00:15:45,817
Let's revive it when we get back to town.

244
00:15:45,900 --> 00:15:48,076
I'm sure Pina would want it that way.

245
00:15:48,680 --> 00:15:49,510
Okay.

246
00:15:56,140 --> 00:15:57,300
Is something wrong?

247
00:15:57,560 --> 00:15:59,357
Whoever's hiding out there, come out.

248
00:15:59,440 --> 00:16:00,270
Now.

249
00:16:04,980 --> 00:16:05,810
Rosalia?

250
00:16:05,893 --> 00:16:08,409
If you saw through my
hiding skill so easy,

251
00:16:08,540 --> 00:16:11,599
your detection skill must
be really high, Swordsman.

252
00:16:12,680 --> 00:16:16,977
Ooh, it looks like you were successful
getting your hands on the Name Flower.

253
00:16:17,060 --> 00:16:18,001
Congratulations.

254
00:16:18,820 --> 00:16:21,160
Now, hand it over before you get hurt.

255
00:16:21,520 --> 00:16:23,108
What are you talking about?

256
00:16:23,340 --> 00:16:25,700
No one's handing anything over, Rosalia.

257
00:16:26,080 --> 00:16:27,000
Not to you.

258
00:16:27,160 --> 00:16:28,257
Or the Orange Gill.

259
00:16:28,340 --> 00:16:30,320
Or should I say Titan's hand?

260
00:16:30,800 --> 00:16:32,388
You're their leader, right?

261
00:16:32,600 --> 00:16:33,430
Nice.

262
00:16:34,080 --> 00:16:35,609
Rosalia's cursor is green.

263
00:16:35,800 --> 00:16:36,940
It's an easy trick.

264
00:16:37,480 --> 00:16:39,656
The green members find their victims.

265
00:16:39,940 --> 00:16:43,817
Then they lure them straight to
the orange players for the ambush.

266
00:16:43,900 --> 00:16:47,960
That was one of your pals last night
eavesdropping on us, wasn't it?

267
00:16:48,460 --> 00:16:52,197
Then the reason you were in that
party with me and the others was to...

268
00:16:52,280 --> 00:16:53,997
How perceptive.

269
00:16:54,080 --> 00:16:58,727
I was observing their strength and watching
them earn all that beautiful money.

270
00:17:01,200 --> 00:17:05,357
You were who I was excited about, and
I was so sad when you left the party.

271
00:17:05,440 --> 00:17:08,381
But then you told me you
were getting a rare item.

272
00:17:08,500 --> 00:17:12,057
What I want to know is if you knew
about us, why did you bring her here?

273
00:17:12,140 --> 00:17:15,728
Are you dumb, or does she have
you wrapped around her finger?

274
00:17:16,740 --> 00:17:18,560
Nope, you're wrong both times.

275
00:17:19,060 --> 00:17:21,942
See, I've been looking
all over for you, Rosalia.

276
00:17:22,520 --> 00:17:24,140
What are you talking about?

277
00:17:24,580 --> 00:17:28,177
Remember ten days ago, you attacked
a guild called the Silver Flags?

278
00:17:28,260 --> 00:17:29,640
The leader survived.

279
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:30,940
Four didn't.

280
00:17:31,280 --> 00:17:33,400
Oh, the losers with no money.

281
00:17:33,780 --> 00:17:35,557
Their leader went back and forth,

282
00:17:35,640 --> 00:17:38,397
from the warp point to the
front lines morning till night.

283
00:17:38,480 --> 00:17:43,097
And with tears in his eyes, he begged
everyone he met to avenge his dead friends.

284
00:17:43,180 --> 00:17:44,980
But he didn't want you killed.

285
00:17:45,400 --> 00:17:47,780
No, he wanted you to go to prison.

286
00:17:48,620 --> 00:17:50,920
Do you have any idea how he felt?

287
00:17:51,580 --> 00:17:52,600
Can't say I do.

288
00:17:53,240 --> 00:17:55,122
Only idiots take this seriously.

289
00:17:55,640 --> 00:17:57,457
So what if we kill someone here?

290
00:17:57,540 --> 00:18:00,481
There's no proof dying
here means you're dead IRL.

291
00:18:00,680 --> 00:18:03,974
Anyway, it's time you started
worrying about yourselves.

292
00:18:13,820 --> 00:18:15,761
Kirito, there's too many of them.

293
00:18:15,920 --> 00:18:17,317
We should get out of here.

294
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:18,340
No, it's okay.

295
00:18:18,600 --> 00:18:20,117
You'll be safe if you stay here.

296
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:22,376
Keep the crystal handy till I say so.

297
00:18:22,620 --> 00:18:25,420
Okay, but...

298
00:18:26,100 --> 00:18:26,930
Kirito!

299
00:18:27,900 --> 00:18:28,730
Kirito?

300
00:18:29,740 --> 00:18:32,240
Dressed in black, one-handed, no shield.

301
00:18:32,660 --> 00:18:35,020
Holy crap, it's the Black Swordsman!

302
00:18:36,460 --> 00:18:37,520
Rosalia, that guy!

303
00:18:37,800 --> 00:18:40,137
He's the beater who plays
solo on the front lines!

304
00:18:40,220 --> 00:18:41,697
He's with the assault team!

305
00:18:41,780 --> 00:18:42,920
No way he is!

306
00:18:43,340 --> 00:18:46,517
Why would someone from the assault
team be all the way down here?

307
00:18:46,600 --> 00:18:51,100
Go on, take him out, and
take everything he owns! Die!

308
00:19:00,040 --> 00:19:02,400
I've got to save him. He won't last.

309
00:19:07,480 --> 00:19:08,580
What's going on?

310
00:19:15,840 --> 00:19:18,917
What the hell you idiots tell him already?

311
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:24,497
410 seconds give or take
that's about the total

312
00:19:24,580 --> 00:19:28,477
damage the seven of you
can inflict on me I'm

313
00:19:28,560 --> 00:19:34,297
level 78 I got 14 500 hp
my battle healing skill

314
00:19:34,380 --> 00:19:37,400
will auto-regenerate 600
points every 10 seconds.

315
00:19:38,300 --> 00:19:41,712
We could stand here all day
and you wouldn't get anywhere.

316
00:19:41,940 --> 00:19:43,980
That's not possible, wanna bet?

317
00:19:44,500 --> 00:19:47,500
If your numbers are high
enough, you're invincible.

318
00:19:47,740 --> 00:19:50,740
Miss that use leveling
systems are unfair that way.

319
00:19:52,500 --> 00:19:55,037
My client spent his entire fortune on this

320
00:19:55,120 --> 00:19:57,437
warp crystal and he'll
get his money's worth.

321
00:19:57,520 --> 00:20:00,285
It's been set to the
coordinates of the prison.

322
00:20:00,620 --> 00:20:03,091
And I'm sending all of you bastards there.

323
00:20:04,820 --> 00:20:07,996
Well, I'm green, and if you
hurt me, you'll go orange.

324
00:20:13,980 --> 00:20:15,680
I'm a solo player, got it.

325
00:20:16,260 --> 00:20:19,907
I don't care if I have to play
as orange for a couple of days.

326
00:20:26,200 --> 00:20:27,700
I'm really sorry, Silica.

327
00:20:28,220 --> 00:20:31,357
This whole time, I was using
you as bait to catch him.

328
00:20:31,440 --> 00:20:34,911
I thought you'd be scared if
I told you the truth about me.

329
00:20:36,360 --> 00:20:40,460
I could never be scared of you,
because you're a good person.

330
00:20:43,080 --> 00:20:45,180
Um, do you really have to go?

331
00:20:45,760 --> 00:20:49,200
Yeah, I've been away from the
front lines for five days.

332
00:20:49,500 --> 00:20:50,620
I need to get back.

333
00:20:52,480 --> 00:20:55,260
I, I think it's Koya
with the assault team.

334
00:20:55,680 --> 00:20:58,621
I could try for a hundred
years and never make it.

335
00:21:02,360 --> 00:21:03,317
Um, I...

336
00:21:03,400 --> 00:21:05,400
You know, levels are just numbers.

337
00:21:05,580 --> 00:21:08,992
And a person's strength in
this world is just an illusion.

338
00:21:09,780 --> 00:21:13,956
Sure, it's cool and all, but there
are more important things than that.

339
00:21:14,700 --> 00:21:16,818
We should meet up in the real world.

340
00:21:17,060 --> 00:21:18,178
That would be cool.

341
00:21:18,420 --> 00:21:20,655
Because I like having you as a friend.

342
00:21:22,700 --> 00:21:24,160
Okay, we will.

343
00:21:24,700 --> 00:21:25,530
I promise.

344
00:21:26,160 --> 00:21:29,200
Well, ready to revive Pina? Yeah!

345
00:21:43,260 --> 00:21:47,820
Pina, when you get back, I'll have
lots of stuff to tell you about.

346
00:21:50,300 --> 00:21:52,720
About the amazing adventure I had.

347
00:21:58,640 --> 00:22:00,157
And about this one day?

348
00:22:00,240 --> 00:22:03,460
When I got to have my
very own big brother!

349
00:22:17,000 --> 00:22:20,140
I don't know.

350
00:23:04,120 --> 00:23:09,640
I'm in front of the heart of my heart

351
00:23:11,120 --> 00:23:17,117
Even though I'm dreaming I'm not going to

352
00:23:17,200 --> 00:23:18,617
be a dream I'm in a

353
00:23:18,700 --> 00:23:21,877
deep state
